l Furby  was released in 1998 the 12 months  following its release a total of 27  million Furbies were sold that's a lot  of Furbies the original Furby was hard  plastic that had plush furry exterior it  had wide somewhat creepy eyes and a beak  that would open and shut the furbies  ears also could wiggle up and down the  toy was advertised with the slogan the  more you play the more they say the  commercial showed kids trying to teach  their Furby their own names and the  names of the owners strangely enough the  toy was advertised almost as a baby doll  toy even though the Furby looked like  some kind of space alien or gremlins  the McDonald's Furbys which were given  out in Happy Meals from March 26 to a  predict they didn't talk or move on  their own  but if you pressed a button their ears  eyes toes and their beaks would move not  that McDonald's version was also maybe a  bit less creepy looking than the real  thing so perhaps it would be a good  alternative if your Furby was giving you  nightmares  but he still wanted to fit in  unfortunately or maybe fortunately the  Furby trend went away pretty fast and it  seems to be unlikely that it will come  back anytime soon Toy Story Toy Story is  a Disney Pixar phenomenon well known to  Millennials the first movie was released  in 1995 and is about toys who when their  owner Andy is asleep come to life  woody Andy's favorite feels jealous when  Buzz Lightyear's  added to Andy's toy collection but by  the end they becomes good friends there  are three toy story movies and they all  follow the adventure of these toy  characters with Buzz and Woody being the  main protagonists when Toy Story 3 was  released in 2010 the younger generations  got to learn about the exciting  Adventures of Woody and Buzz following  the 1999 release of Toy Story 2  McDonald's released their collection of  Toy Story toys Toy Story is a beloved  Disney Pixar movie so it was no surprise  that the McDonald's toys were popular  too toy story 2 wa